<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine 1996/97 wheat sales 8.0-8.3 mln T-source.</title>
<headline>Argentine 1996/97 wheat sales 8.0-8.3 mln T-source.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine exporters had sold between 8,027,000 tonnes and 8,327,000 tonnes of 1996/97 wheat by February 20, a market source said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The source provided the following table of sales,</p>
<p>including comparative figures for last season (figures in</p>
<p>tonnes):</p>
<p>			1996/97		    1995/96</p>
<p>    Algeria	 200,000</p>
<p>    Bolivia	  50,000		     80,000</p>
<p>    Brazil	1,950,000		  3,000,000</p>
<p>    Bulgaria*     120,000/420,000</p>
<p>    Cameroon	 15,000</p>
<p>    Chile	    75,000		     40,000</p>
<p>    China	    50,000		     30,000</p>
<p>    Colombia	 75,000</p>
<p>    Croatia	  55,000</p>
<p>    Cuba	    200,000</p>
<p>    Cyprus	   25,000</p>
<p>    Dominican Rep. 50,000</p>
<p>    Ecuador	  15,000</p>
<p>    Egypt	   600,000</p>
<p>    Estonia	  55,000</p>
<p>    Georgia	  50,000</p>
<p>    Greece	   25,000</p>
<p>    India	   100,000</p>
<p>    Indonesia     350,000		    180,000</p>
<p>    Iran	    800,000		    100,000</p>
<p>    Iraq	    150,000</p>
<p>    Israel	   20,000</p>
<p>    Italy	   100,000</p>
<p>    Jordan	  250,000</p>
<p>    Kenya	   160,000</p>
<p>    Lesotho	  10,000</p>
